{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>He brings up</b> — it is written in Jeremiah: is there among the vanities of the nations those who cause rain, and if the heavens in their generation give showers — only all is by the will of HaShem. So too Job said: who does great things beyond search, and after Him who gives rain." "<b>Vapors</b> — the mist of the earth that rises." "And the sense of <b>from the ends of the earth</b> is opposite <b>from the ends of the heavens</b> is its going out, for the sphere has no beginning, only opposite the horizontal and opposite what is adjacent to it — and these are the senses from every place." "And the sense of <b>lightnings</b> — for they are fire with rain, which is water, and the lammed in <b>for rain</b> is causal, and the sense of <b>treasuries for the wind</b> is that they are in potentiality, for potentiality is a stored thing. Thus it is established that <b>all that He pleases He does</b>, and this is one proof, and a second proof is the signs of HaShem in Egypt. And he mentioned first the plague of the firstborn, for two reasons: the first, that the essence of our exodus from Egypt was because of the plague of the firstborn, as it is written, <b>Behold, I will slay your firstborn son</b>. And the second, because the firstborn of Israel were spared, and this was a miracle within a miracle."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 135, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra appears to paraphrase Jeremiah 14:22 rather than quote it verbatim.", 2 "The term המחל is obscure here; rendered hyper-literally as 'the horizontal,' though the word is unusual and may reflect a corruption or technical term."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:49.840932340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}